# E06 Yellow Pages: parallel. The searches of the first clients leave at their setup, as the registrations of the
# providers: a search that reaches the broker before any provider of its service gets no answer, and the client never
# asks again; which ones depends on the interleaving, in the C# as in the C++. Compared: the registrations, searches and
# unregistration as multisets, the forced unregistration, and as many requests, responses and results as answered
# searches (the clients added for the last run are always answered).
cover all
fact register ^\t\[(provider\d) -> broker\]: register (Add|Sub)$
fact search ^\t\[(client\d) -> broker\]: search (Add|Sub)$
fact unregister ^\t\[(provider\d) -> broker\]: unregister (Add|Sub)$
fact force ^\t\[provider1 -> provider1\]: force-unregister$
fact providers ^\t\[broker -> (client\d)\]: providers (.*)$
fact request ^\t\[(client\d) -> (provider\d)\]: request (\d+) (\d+)$
fact response ^\t\[(provider\d) -> (client\d)\]: response (-?\d+)$
fact result ^\[(client\d)\]: (Add|Sub)\((\d+), (\d+)\) = (-?\d+)$
same register bag
same search bag
same unregister bag
same force count
check providers count in [2,6]
check request count == providers.count
check response count == request.count
check result count == response.count
check result distinct(0) >= 2
